{"skill":{"slug":"gemini-image-gen","displayName":"Gemini Image Gen"},"version":{"version":"1.3.1","createdAt":1771230230797,"changelog":"- Added guidance for integrating with the opencode-omo skill for workflow/pipeline image generation.\n- Updated documentation to mention opencode-omo in the integration section.\n- No changes to core image generation features or CLI options.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"HEARTBEAT.md","size":1014,"sha256":"7b86fa43f4fe22917f14dc6fa6b4f89785266c376d64179f1314424a2fe44fbb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"INSTALL.md","size":1504,"sha256":"b1f7b1b7e57f4c8e939214fe39f176855c2d5a3523b6f5cb06aef8293f70124a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":2898,"sha256":"e76e4d780c3e2c02a7ca06ad524b454c6daa6dba47815f17ecee587923d1840b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4640,"sha256":"85a9b7a58aad6e877ef50be5f93a80248aa4b1817a01059d47ef6be630b6b070","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"package.json","size":2512,"sha256":"bada1a428160328e19fcc9bbf195fdb9114558f01926594de12d8192a4809cd7","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/gen.py","size":14913,"sha256":"a75a78afbb3b1142076d136abd454cea9a419acc76dc947b3f4636dc47855627","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2399,"sha256":"05ff26f437aaec64e70deda81feefeed5ef9903ac3531ec9b997a8b984b23268","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789032267791,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b427186be8c7b93c763a325b254ac009daae87a2ea225e4098b4632ed34735ee","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b427186be8c7b93c763a325b254ac009daae87a2ea225e4098b4632ed34735ee","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: gemini-image-gen\nVersion: 1.3.1\n\nThe `scripts/gen.py` file contains a data exfiltration vulnerability. The `--edit` argument, intended for image editing, allows reading arbitrary files from the local filesystem via `load_image_as_base64`. The base64-encoded content of these files is then sent to the Google Gemini API (generativelanguage.googleapis.com) as part of the image editing request. This flaw could be exploited by a malicious prompt to exfiltrate sensitive local files to a third-party service.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161235419},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":80,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":11,"checkedAt":1789032267791},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly does image generation as advertised, but its heartbeat guidance can prompt public posting, avatar changes, and memory saving without clear user-controlled approval boundaries.","dimensions":[{"detail":"GEMINI_API_KEY, outbound access to generativelanguage.googleapis.com, reading user-specified edit images, and writing generated files are proportionate for image generation, but users should avoid sensitive prompts/images unless they accept third-party processing.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documented install and update paths use unpinned npx clawhub commands, which is a mutable supply-chain execution path; manual git clone is also documented and no sudo or privilege escalation is requested.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The runtime guidance does not require explicit just-in-time confirmation before public/account-affecting actions or memory persistence, and the documentation under-discloses that prompts and edited images are sent to Google's API.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The script does not install services, hooks, or backdoors, but HEARTBEAT.md instructs saving good results to memory and suggests account-visible avatar/social changes without scoped retention or approval controls.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The core Python tool coherently generates or edits images using Gemini/Imagen and writes local outputs, but HEARTBEAT.md extends the behavior to social posting, profile avatar updates, and memory retention based on vague agent judgment.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing. Use it only with prompts and images you are willing to send to Google, avoid opening or publishing generated galleries from untrusted prompts until captions are escaped, and do not let heartbeat workflows post publicly, change avatars, or save memories unless each action is explicitly approved. Prefer a pinned or otherwise verified ClawHub installer/update path.","findings":"[P6] expected: Downgraded as a false positive: scripts/gen.py returns a list of generated creative prompts, not system prompts or hidden instructions.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted for HEARTBEAT.md: social posting, avatar updates, and memory saving go beyond local image generation and are not bounded by explicit user confirmation.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted for HEARTBEAT.md account/publication effects and memory persistence; these actions may be related integrations, but the approval and retention boundaries are too vague.\n[RP1] expected: Accepted as an install-path risk rather than malicious behavior: npx install/update commands are normal for this ecosystem but are unpinned and mutable.\n[LP3] expected: Partially accepted: the needed env, network, file read, and file write capabilities fit the image-generation purpose, but explicit permission scoping is limited.\n[SQP-2] expected: Accepted as under-disclosure: Google API use is stated, but the docs do not plainly warn that prompts and edited image bytes leave the local machine.\n[SDI-2] expected: Downgraded for environment access: GEMINI_API_KEY is declared in SKILL.md and package.json and is expected for Gemini API use.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a real implementation weakness: the generated HTML gallery inserts prompt text without escaping, enabling stored HTML/script injection if an attacker controls a prompt and the gallery is opened or hosted.\n[T08] expected: Accepted as supply-chain exposure in the documented npx install/update commands, not evidence of embedded malicious code in the reviewed artifact.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789032267791}}}}}